1
00:00:36,830 --> 00:00:42,470
[She's Wild Fire]

2
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:47,710
[Episode 14: Please Don't Leave Me Again]

3
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:16,120
You're awake?

4
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:20,800
Sweetheart,

5
00:01:21,330 --> 00:01:22,610
why'd you fall asleep?

6
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:23,520
Mom,

7
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:26,160
is Dad your general?

8
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:27,120
He's not Dad.

9
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:28,800
He's Uncle Chu.

10
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:31,000
Why did you ask?

11
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:34,560
Because he came to play with me
this afternoon.

12
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:38,039
I heard him on the phone.
He sounded really tough.

13
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:41,039
He was talking some sense into
those bad people at the factory,

14
00:01:41,039 --> 00:01:43,960
so they wouldn't dare do anything bad.

15
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:45,520
And

16
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:47,200
he said

17
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:50,920
you would fight the big monsters up front,

18
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:54,080
and he's in charge of
protecting the supplies.

19
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:55,200
Mom,

20
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,920
what are supplies?

21
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:58,720
Is it something yummy?

22
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,039
It's gotta be Dad.

23
00:02:10,039 --> 00:02:13,200
He said he's coming to race me tonight.

24
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:22,570
Where's Nannan?

25
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:25,800
Nannan.

26
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:29,600
Dad.

27
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:31,480
Did you have fun today?

28
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:32,280
Yes.

29
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,320
Then give Dad a kiss.

30
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:36,680
What a good boy.

31
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:42,040
I brought some shredded chicken congee
from the corner shop.

32
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:43,720
I remember how much Nannan loves it.

33
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:47,780
And I figured I'd bring some supplies
for my "commander-in-chief," too.

34
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:55,400
Dad,

35
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:58,240
can my toy car turn into a boat?

36
00:02:58,560 --> 00:02:59,800
Of course it can.

37
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:01,800
But

38
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:05,000
we'll need a little magic.

39
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:06,800
How about this:

40
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,600
let's figure it out together.

41
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,400
Then I'll show you.

42
00:03:11,530 --> 00:03:12,680
You'll show me?

43
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:13,200
Okay.

44
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:36,720
Nannan is asleep?

45
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:38,720
I have something to tell you.

46
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:46,480
Nannan

47
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,160
is your son.

48
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:02,680
My

49
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:04,880
son?

50
00:04:20,170 --> 00:04:21,730
So does that mean

51
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:25,920
you've forgiven

52
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,530
the man I was 5 years ago?

53
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,640
Don't leave me behind again

54
00:04:50,130 --> 00:04:51,460
like you did 5 years ago.

55
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:11,880
Ms. Xie, bad news!

56
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:12,720
No, wait.

57
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:13,680
It's great news!

58
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:14,060
It's booming!

59
00:06:14,060 --> 00:06:14,880
It's completely booming!

60
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:15,520
The orders—

61
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:17,250
they're pouring in like crazy!

62
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:19,200
Our projected capacity
for the affordable line

63
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:21,240
can't even cover a tenth of the demand.

64
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:22,570
What should we do, Ms. Xie?

65
00:06:22,570 --> 00:06:23,530
Tell everyone

66
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:26,520
that we're no longer accepting

67
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:28,560
any prospective orders
without signed contracts.

68
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,520
Ms. Xie,

69
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:31,160
with things taking off like this,

70
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:33,420
it seems like a shame to turn orders away.

71
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:35,280
When a wave comes crashing in,

72
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:38,680
the ones who rush in first are
often the first to get stranded.

73
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,200
We can ride the wave,

74
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,600
but we'll

75
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:43,040
set our own pace.

76
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,320
Time to get to work.

77
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:10,200
Okay.

78
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:16,120
Try this.

79
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:17,680
It's their specialty—

80
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,540
thin wrapper, plenty of filling.

81
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:29,520
You can read the documents anytime,

82
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:32,000
but it'll be a shame
if the food gets cold.

83
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:42,920
What's wrong?

84
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:43,900
Not your taste?

85
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:46,600
Eating is like fueling a machine.

86
00:07:46,730 --> 00:07:49,130
As long as it runs,
that's all that matters.

87
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:53,370
Then you still have to
put the right fuel in it.

88
00:07:53,370 --> 00:07:55,490
Think about it. Is there anything

89
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,840
you can eat that gives you a real boost?

90
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,400
Radish cake.

91
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,760
I used to love the ones

92
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:09,960
from that little shop by the old street.

93
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,480
But the owner moved away,

94
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,760
and I haven't had them since.

95
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:16,520
Okay.

96
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,370
Where are you going?

97
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,600
Don't go out of your way to get it.

98
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:26,000
For you, I'll always find a way.

99
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,600
What's a little radish cake?

100
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:28,300
Wait for me.

101
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:30,000
No.

102
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,680
You won't be able to find it.

103
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,679
That place has a flavor all its own.

104
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:36,520
The savory flavor is just right,

105
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,039
and

106
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:38,720
they even cure their own Chinese sausage.

107
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:42,980
Even if you tried to buy some,
you'd never find
one that tastes quite the same.

108
00:08:47,800 --> 00:09:02,800
♪ Happy Birthday to You ♪

109
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:05,080
Happy birthday.

110
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:06,000
Make a wish, okay?

111
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:06,600
Nannan?

112
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:09,920
I wish I could spend every birthday

113
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:12,080
with Mom and Dad.

114
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:16,120
Of course.

115
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:20,280
Now blow out the candles.

116
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:20,920
Come on.

117
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,600
Happy birthday!
